[quote="Raccoonoo"]

It&#39;s very difficult to play tabletop RPGs on your own 
[/quote]


That&#39;s not compltely true, though it takes a bit of extra work to simulate the GM. There&#39;s a <a href="https://boardgamegeek.com/guild/1999">whole guld on BGG</a> dedicated to soloing popular (and obscure) RPGs.&nbsp; The key is to find a way of simulating a GM, and there are a number of tools out there that can help with that. 

That said it can be a bit much, particularly for someone new to RPGs.&nbsp;

 I&#39;ve started soloing the Starter Kit adventure, you can find my session notes here if you&#39;re interested:&nbsp;&nbsp; <a href="https://boardgamegeek.com/geeklist/241610/item/6207548#item6207548"> https://boardgamegeek.com/geeklist/241610/item/6207548#item6207548 </a>

